-- title:
--   Zariski-local infinitesimal lifting along smooth morphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $f \colon X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes with $S$ affine and $f$ smooth, let $C$ be a commutative ring and $J \subseteq C$ an ideal that is nilpotent in the lattice of ideals (so $J^n = 0$ for some $n$). Let $t \colon \operatorname{Spec} C \to S$ be a morphism and $x_0 \colon \operatorname{Spec}(C/J) \to X$ a morphism which is compatible with $t$ in the sense that $x_0$ followed by $f$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $C \to C/J$ followed by $t$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an index type $\iota$ (in the same universe) and a family $a \colon \iota \to C$ whose range generates the unit ideal, $\operatorname{span}(\operatorname{range} a) = \top$, such that for every $i \in \iota$, writing $A_i = C[1/a_i]$ for the away-localisation and $J_i = J A_i$ for the ideal generated by the image of $J$, there is a morphism $x \colon \operatorname{Spec} A_i \to X$ with: $x$ followed by $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(C \to A_i)$ followed by $t$; and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $A_i \to A_i/J_i$ followed by $x$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the induced map $C/J \to A_i/J_i$ followed by $x_0$. Thus $x_0$ lifts to an $S$-morphism after base change to each member of a standard affine open cover of $\operatorname{Spec} C$, compatibly with $x_0$ modulo $J_i$.
--
--   This is the Zariski-local form of the infinitesimal lifting criterion for smooth morphisms: the lift of a point modulo a nilpotent ideal exists not necessarily globally on $\operatorname{Spec} C$, but on the standard opens of a cover indexed by a family generating the unit ideal. It is used downstream to produce local lifts that are then glued, in the construction of liftings for fake elliptic curves in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting and in the study of the relative group law on Jacobians with good reduction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Smooth_exists_span_eq_top_and_forall_exists_lift_away_of_isNilpotent.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
